WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.560
So here is some palladium wire. It is a very,
very small

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:08.870
sample of palladium wire. But we will get
it out and see what

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:09.870
we can find out.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:13.799
Palladium is a material, or an element, that
is quite similar to

00:00:13.799 --> 00:00:21.930
platinum so most of these metals, so called
noble metals, or

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:26.620
platinum-group metals are found in South Africa
and they are

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.120
the main supplier, the mines in South Africa.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:37.940
In fact it is so small I can hardly see it.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:43.840
Palladium is a compound which has recently
become much

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:48.870
more widely used by chemists because palladium
metal and

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:54.320
palladium compounds are used widely in organic
chemistry,

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:58.470
that is the chemistry of carbon compounds,
for joining

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:02.220
different groups together with a bond, two
carbon atoms, the

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:07.120
so called Heck reactions. So most of my colleagues
who do

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:10.200
organic chemistry at some stage or another
employ this

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.020
reaction of palladium.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:15.409
So this is a small sample of palladium. Palladium
is used to

00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:18.830
make electrodes; it’s also used for forming
electrical circuits.

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:22.710
It is a very, very, very expensive metal:
it is a precious metal.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:27.310
It is refined from ores from South Africa,
Australia and also

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:30.869
the former Soviet Republic. The price of palladium
has gone

00:01:30.869 --> 00:01:34.170
down recently though, because it is ored with
platinum and

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.630
the value of platinum or the demand for platinum
has gone

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:41.650
up because of auto-catalytic converters. Palladium
is used to

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:46.920
catalyse organic reactions but also the electrode
surface in

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:50.270
electro-chemical processes. I’ve got some
other samples of

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:51.270
palladium elsewhere there.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:55.780
It is also used in the pharmaceutical industry,
but again there

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:59.960
it is not quite such a good reaction because
you have to

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:05.250
remove all traces of palladium from the products
at the end.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:09.920
So there are other ways that people use it.
In my own work, I

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:13.810
have used, or my students have used, palladium
quite widely

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:17.630
as a catalyst for adding hydrogen to organic
compounds, so

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:20.290
again it’s is one of the elements that’s
have really been quite

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:20.780
good to me.

